        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "93016c9a-921d-50fd-a787-445b90d1c45c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Schlegel, Frank De Winne, Dirk Frimout\n- Organizations: ESA, NASA, Belgian Air Component, Roscosmos\n- Missions: NASA Space Shuttle missions, ISS Expedition 21, ISS Expedition 35, Soyuz TMA-08M\n- Places: Überlingen, Ledeberg, Belgium, International Space Station\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Schlegel was born in Überlingen on 3 August 1951.\n- Hans Schlegel is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Frank De Winne was born on 25 April 1961 in Ledeberg, Belgium.\n- Frank De Winne is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\n- Frank De Winne became Belgium's second person in space after Dirk Frimout.\n- In 2009, Frank De Winne became the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.\n- ISS Expedition 35 was only the second ISS crew led by neither a NASA astronaut nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after ISS Expedition 21 in 2009 under Frank De Winne's command.\n- Soyuz TMA-08M transported three members of the Expedition 35 crew to the International Space Station.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a16bad85-653a-5a7e-857d-423499b82c8b",
        "text": "Page: Hans Schlegel. Sentence: Hans Wilhelm Schlegel (Überlingen, 3 August 1951) is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: Frank, Viscount De Winne (born 25 April 1961, in Ledeberg, Belgium) is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He is Belgium's second person in space (after Dirk Frimout).\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He was the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.\nPage: Expedition 35. Sentence: Expedition 35 was also only the second time an ISS crew is led by neither a NASA astronaut, nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 in 2009, when ESA astronaut Frank De Winne was in command.\nPage: Soyuz TMA-08M. Sentence: It transported three members of the Expedition 35 crew to the International Space Station.",
